{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfLU4pQxwYWZ7uDKTLUd3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the planning task. My plan is provided above via the final structured output.\n\nA note on process integrity: I attempted to open `evals/live.py` and its test/grader files through the read interface, but the host returned only acknowledgements without file bodies. Rather than fabricate the current implementation, I grounded the plan in the material actually provided — the request, manifest, pinned v0.3.0 contract, and the `docs/decisions.md` ADR log (itself a Definition Pack reference that describes the live tier in ADR‑007/015/016/018/019) — and recorded the un-inspectable source as the first and most consequential planning gap.\n\nThe plan stays within the stated objective (restructuring the live-eval runner for three isolated, separately-graded stages while preserving quota-aware checkpointing, resumability, and completed-trial semantics), flags that the request's core terms have no authority source in the Definition Pack, and surfaces six structured `GAP:` findings covering the inspection failure, the definition insufficiency, the provider-quota ambiguity (ADR‑018 vs ADR‑019), the diff-allowlist scope risk, and the golden-case/oracle-envelope uncertainty."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8927,"cache_read_input_tokens":79157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8927},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e50d584e-123f-4980-866d-dc91f0c11466","uuid":"8c73570a-0004-4280-b04e-8933197f739b","request_id":"req_011CfLU4kzLN9UQyHkKz4AHh"}
