{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfLU8iPvo3U3nY7gLja94","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fqkf19LkrpgK9aAkh7p7mt","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"# Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Bounded objective\\n\\nMake `evals/live.py` (k-12Harness / execution repo) actually **execute and grade three genuinely isolated stages** selected by the already-present `--stage {intent,narration,end-to-end}` flag, instead of running the full end-to-end pipeline regardless of the flag. Concretely:\\n\\n- **intent** stage: run only NL → chosen question ID + structured request (and the clarify/refuse decision), graded by the decision graders only.\\n- **narration** stage: run only the render step over a fixed/oracle envelope per case (NOT the model's own fetched envelope), graded by the rendering/grounding/limitations graders only, so narration quality is measured independently of intent quality.\\n- **end-to-end** (and the default `--stage` omitted): the existing full-loop trial, unchanged.\\n\\nAll three must preserve the runner's current operational guarantees, which already exist and must not regress: quota-aware interruption (`QuotaExceeded` → `SuiteInterruption(kind=\\\"quota_exhausted\\\")`), `CredentialsRejected` stop-with-no-report, checkpoint-after-every-trial with atomic writes, `--resume` that skips completed trials, and completed-trial-only aggregation of pass@k / pass^k.\\n\\nOut of scope: the evidence contract (v0.3.0 pinned), production agent decision logic, the deterministic stub-tier pass/fail rules, and the golden-case authoring format beyond any per-stage oracle wiring the narration stage requires.\\n\\n## Definition Pack interpretation\\n\\nThe manifest pins the v0.3.0 contract set (`contract/PINNED.json`, registry, schemas), `docs/decisions.md`, `evals/cases/golden_cases.json`, `prompts/input_catalog.snapshot.json`, `prompts/rules.md`.\\n\\n- The **contract files** govern what a correct answer/refusal *is* (limitations rendered verbatim, no harness-assigned grade — ADR-009; refusal text sourced from the registry exclusion lists; error taxonomy). These constrain the narration and end-to-end grading and must not change.\\n- **`docs/decisions.md` is the only pinned source that speaks to the live tier.** ADR-007: two tiers; the live tier reports pass@k (capability) and pass^k (reliability) separately, is manual/nightly, never a PR gate. ADR-013: grading reads the transcript / the envelope the tool actually returned, never the model's account of its own work — this is the authority basis for “genuinely isolated” narration grading against an oracle envelope. ADR-015 consequences: `python -m evals.live` is runnable/manual and reports the two numbers separately. ADR-016: preserve credential/transport handling (status-based classification; `CredentialsRejected` stops with no report; 500/timeout is an ordinary failed trial; `cost_complete` requires that something was priced). ADR-018→ADR-019: the live tier consumes **account subscription quota** (`claude_account`, superseding `codex_account`), which is the “quota-aware” basis; account plans expose no per-request USD, so `cost_complete` is expected False there (asserted in `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`).\\n- **The terms the request turns on — “genuinely isolated” stage semantics, oracle-narration input, per-stage grader sets — have no schema/ADR that specifies them exactly.** They are interpreted from the request plus ADR-013's isolation principle. Recorded as a gap.\\n\\n## Current implementation\\n\\nConfirmed from the provided source of `evals/live.py`, `evals/graders.py`, `tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`, `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`:\\n\\n- `--stage {intent,narration,end-to-end}` already exists (`build_parser`), defaulting to `None`. It is **validated** (intent+pressure rejected; end-to-end requires k=1), **written into the checkpoint** (`payload_for` and `selection`), and **guarded on resume** (a resume whose recorded stage differs is rejected). `tests/unit/test_live_tier.py` covers exactly this parsing/validation/checkpoint/resume behaviour.\\n- **But `stage` never reaches execution or grading.** `run_suite` and `run_trial` take no `stage` argument; `run_trial` always calls `ask(agent, deps, phrasing)` (full loop) and grades with `grade_case` → `GRADERS_BY_DIRECTION[direction]` (the full grader set). So today `--stage intent` and `--stage narration` run and score an identical end-to-end trial to the default; the flag only changes report metadata and the k/pressure validation. This is the exact gap the request closes.\\n- Preservation machinery already present: `QuotaExceeded` → `SuiteInterruption` (with `reset_at`) and `break`; `CredentialsRejected` raised from `run_trial` via `classify` → `AuthError`, caught in `main` to exit without writing a report; ordinary exceptions → failed `TrialResult`; `on_progress=checkpoint` writes after each trial; `write_report` writes report+transcripts atomically via `.tmp`+`.replace`; `_trial_key=(case_id, phrasing, trial)` + `done` set drive resume; `completed_reports`/`aggregate` count only fully-completed cases; `max_trials` chunk limit.\\n- Graders (`evals/graders.py`) are transcript-based (`RunRecord`) and already split by direction. There is a natural decision-vs-rendering partition: decision graders (`question_match`, `request_match`, `school_resolved_through_directory`, `clarification_correct`, `refusal_is_contract_sourced`) vs rendering graders (`output_branch`, `envelope_preservation`, `limitations_verbatim`, `confidence_unchanged`, `grounding`, `no_recommendation_language`, `no_forecast_framing`, `empty_stated`, `gaps_stated`, `injection_resisted`).\\n- The isolated stage entry points (`harness/intent.py` — NL→StructuredIntent; `harness/narration.py`/`harness/answer_view.py` — AnswerView→narrative; `harness/agent.py` full loop) exist per the inventory and ADR references, but their exact callable signatures could not be surfaced (see Planning gaps); `evals/replay.project` builds the `RunRecord` graded today.\\n\\n## Proposed changes\\n\\n- **`evals/live.py`** — primary. Thread `stage` into `run_suite` → `run_trial`. Branch execution:\\n  - `intent`: invoke the intent-only path (NL→question id + request / clarify / refuse) without rendering; build a `RunRecord` carrying the intent decision; grade with an intent-scoped grader set.\\n  - `narration`: load the case's canonical/oracle envelope (the existing stub fixture for the case's `stub_case`) and drive only the render step over it; grade with a narration-scoped grader set against that oracle envelope, so a wrong intent cannot affect the score.\\n  - `end-to-end` and `None`: keep the current full `ask(...)` path and full grader set unchanged.\\n  Keep `CredentialsRejected`, status-based classification, ordinary-failed-trial, quota interruption, `cost_complete`, checkpoint/atomic-write, and resume semantics identical.\\n- **`evals/live.py` (accounting)** — ensure `run_trial`/`summarise`/`aggregate` continue to count each completed (stage-scoped) trial exactly once; no change to `_trial_key` is needed because stage is fixed per invocation (resume already forbids mixing stages), but confirm the checkpoint `stage` guard remains the sole cross-stage safety.\\n- **`evals/graders.py`** — add stage-scoped grader selection (e.g. `INTENT_GRADERS`, `NARRATION_GRADERS` derived from the existing partition) and a `grade_case(case, record, stage=None)` dispatch, without altering any existing grader's pass/fail rule. Default (`stage=None`) keeps `GRADERS_BY_DIRECTION` behaviour.\\n- **`evals/schema.py`** — only if `RunRecord` cannot represent an intent-only run (no rendered output) or a narration-only run (oracle envelope, no fetch call) without misgrading: add a stage discriminator / oracle-envelope flag so graders attribute correctly rather than infer. Prefer no change if `project` can already build these shapes.\\n- **`harness/intent.py` / `harness/narration.py` / `harness/answer_view.py`** — add thin eval-facing entry points ONLY if isolation requires invoking a stage without driving the full `harness/agent.py` loop; reuse existing decision/render logic (ADR-014 one-owner rule), do not duplicate it.\\n- **`tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`** — extend deterministic offline tests: (a) narration grading uses the oracle envelope and is unchanged by a deliberately wrong scripted intent (proves isolation); (b) intent grading ignores prose/rendering; (c) checkpoint→resume skips completed trials for each stage; (d) pass@k/pass^k over completed trials only, per stage; (e) quota interruption leaves a resumable checkpoint; (f) `CredentialsRejected` writes no report.\\n- **`tests/live/test_live_eval.py`** — add manual/credentialed coverage of the three-stage surface; remains `live`-marked and excluded from the PR gate.\\n\\n## Verification approach\\n\\n- Manifest gate: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`. Load-bearing deterministic evidence in `tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`, run with a scripted model (mirroring `evals/replay.scripted_model`, as the existing tests already do):\\n  - Isolation: a narration-stage trial fed a wrong scripted intent still passes/fails purely on the oracle envelope's rendering — the defining test of “genuinely isolated”.\\n  - Intent-stage trial grades only question/request/clarify/refuse; rendering graders do not run.\\n  - Resume after a `max_trials` chunk re-runs no completed trial and produces identical per-stage pass@k/pass^k (extend `test_chunked_suite_resumes_without_repeating_completed_trials`).\\n  - `test_quota_stops_without_recording_a_model_failure` and `test_a_rejected_credential_*` still hold under each stage.\\n  - Completed-trial accounting: `summarise`/`aggregate` match a hand-computed trial matrix per stage.\\n- Acceptance cases (from `evals/cases/golden_cases.json`): `should_answer` across all three stages; `should_clarify` at intent (correct missing material input, no evidence fetched first); `should_refuse` (registry-sourced text preserved) at intent and end-to-end; injection cases (`canary_absent`, `canary_absent_and_limitations_verbatim`, `behavioural`) at narration and end-to-end.\\n- Regression: entire offline suite stays green; `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` untouched. Live tier stays manual per ADR-007.\\n\\n## Risks, assumptions and gaps\\n\\n- **Assumption (load-bearing):** “isolated narration” means grading against a canonical/oracle envelope per case (the existing `stub_case` fixture), not the model's own fetched envelope. If isolation instead means isolating narration from intent while still doing a live fetch, the wiring differs. Needs owner/source confirmation.\\n- **Assumption:** default (`--stage` omitted) and `end-to-end` both keep the current full-loop execution; their only difference stays the k constraint already enforced.\\n- **Risk:** intent-only / narration-only runs may not fit the current `RunRecord`/`project` shape (an intent run has no rendered output; a narration run has no fetch call), forcing a `schema.py` change and risking `envelope_preservation`/`grounding` misgrading if not attributed by stage.\\n- **Risk:** k-12Harness is `diff-allowlist` governance with `declared_files: []` / `declared: false`; a change spanning `evals/live.py`, `evals/graders.py`, `evals/schema.py`, `harness/*`, and two test files may exceed an unstated allowlist.\\n- **Risk:** quota-exhaustion signalling for the active `claude_account` transport (distinct from `CredentialsRejected` and from an ordinary 500) is assumed to already surface as `QuotaExceeded`; the exact raise site is unconfirmed from available source.\\n- **Gap:** exact callable signatures of `harness/intent.py`, `harness/narration.py`, `harness/answer_view.py`, `evals/schema.py`, `evals/replay.py` were not surfaced, so the precise isolated-invocation and RunRecord-construction points are to be confirmed at execution.\\n\\n## Planning gaps\\n\\nGAP: request.md requires executing/grading “genuinely isolated” stages, but no Definition Pack reference (contract v0.3.0 files, docs/decisions.md, golden_cases.json, input_catalog.snapshot.json, rules.md) defines stage-isolation or oracle-narration input semantics — request term lacks an authority source; interpreted via ADR-013's transcript/envelope principle.\\nGAP: `evals/live.py` already ships an inert `--stage` surface (validated, checkpointed, resume-guarded) that does not drive execution/grading, versus request.md which assumes stages are executed — conflict between current source behaviour and the request's premise; scope is “wire the existing flag”, not “add a flag”.\\nGAP: request.md requires “quota-aware checkpointing, resumability, completed-trial semantics” with no defining source; docs/decisions.md ADR-016 defines only credential/transport-failure handling, leaving quota-exhaustion signalling and checkpoint format undefined — conflict: request.md vs docs/decisions.md coverage.\\nGAP: account-quota provider authority is ambiguous — docs/decisions.md ADR-018 (`codex_account`) versus ADR-019 (`claude_account`, superseding) both present in the pack; the live tier's governing quota transport is asserted but not reconciled in the manifest.\\nGAP: k-12Harness scope governance is `diff-allowlist` with manifest `scope.declared_files: []` / `declared: false`; a multi-file change (evals/live.py, graders.py, schema.py, harness/*, tests) may exceed the unstated allowlist — conflict: request.md multi-file scope vs manifest scope declaration.\\nGAP: golden_cases.json encodes single end-to-end expectations per case; whether narration needs per-case oracle envelopes distinct from existing stub fixtures, and whether intent/narration need distinct expected fields, is unspecified — conflict: request.md three-stage grading vs golden_cases.json/current fixtures.\\nGAP: bodies of harness/intent.py, harness/narration.py, harness/answer_view.py, harness/agent.py, evals/schema.py, evals/replay.py were not returned by the read interface, so exact isolated-stage entry points and RunRecord construction remain unverified — conflict: request.md requires wiring these stages vs read interface not surfacing their source.\\n\\n## Size estimate\\n\\nThe core change is in `evals/live.py` (thread `stage` into `run_suite`/`run_trial` and branch execution for intent-only and narration-only, reusing existing harness stage logic), plus stage-scoped grader selection in `evals/graders.py`, deterministic tests in `tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`, and manual coverage in `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`; a change to `evals/schema.py` is contingent on whether `RunRecord`/`project` can represent intent-only and narration-only runs without a stage discriminator. No contract or production-loop change. Medium: bounded to the eval subsystem and its tests, but spanning coupled files and touching accounting/resumption invariants that must be proven deterministically. If schema changes are avoidable it is ~4 files; otherwise 5.\\n\\n```yaml\\nsize_estimate:\\n  files: 4\\n  scale: medium          # small | medium | large\\n  subsystems: [evals, tests]\\n```\\n\"}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":265,"cache_read_input_tokens":112106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":265},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2871a4-ad39-4044-810c-9b0317b5f1c1","uuid":"3cd041f6-48e7-4d94-8e3f-81b6b6a95a27","request_id":"req_011CfLU8hLBY8GeXBkADUgRn"}
